# Dr. Joachim Dörges, "Life auf dem TI-59", CHIP 9/1980, Programmservice, pp. 37-39.
# For TI-59 with PC-100 printer.
#
# Conway's Game of Life on a 10 x 10 field; the cells outside the field stay
# empty. Every generation is printed inside a frame, a live cell as 0.
# Optional mutations throw a random extra element into the field after each
# printout. It takes part in the next generation but is never printed itself,
# so a lone element dies unseen and only one that lands near a pattern shows.
#
# Keys:
#   E               prepare: clear the field, print the headline
#   row A           choose a row (1-10)
#   column B        set an element in that row (1-10); repeat for further columns
#   C               run without mutation
#   seed D          run with mutation; the seed is a number between 0 and 1
#
# The program never stops by itself: R/S ends a run. E starts over.
# The article notes that a mutation can hit an occupied cell, which then prints
# as 1 or higher instead of 0.
#
# The article gives no start pattern. This preset enters a glider and presses C.
#
# The article: a full field takes 5 min 57 s to compute and 2 min 20 s to print;
# an empty field 27 s and 8 s.
#
# Registers (the article's table; those it only calls occupied read from the program):
#   R00-R06  indexes, counters, scratch    R10-R17  frame print codes
#   R18      row pointer                   R19-R28  rows 1 to 10
#   R30-R32  rows being summed             R33      sum L
#   R34-R36  columns being summed          R37      sum M
#   R38      L, for working out M          R39      current row
#   R40      column index                  R41      deaths N and births P
#   R42      previous row's N and P        R45      random number
#   R46      constant 1117
# A row is stored as 0.0000100000: one decimal digit per column.
# Flag 1 is the mutation switch.
#
# The article loads the program from two cards (card 2 only for mutations) and
# keys in 5 Op 17. The preset's partition does the same.

MODEL: TI-59
PRINTER: on
PARTITION: 559.49

CUECARD:
Template: MagnetCard
Title: LIFE (CHIP 9/1980)
A: row
B: column
C: run
D: seed, run
E: clear

